  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0085_f2f5f53b9cbc.png\" style=\"width: 728px; height: 294px;\" /></p><p>The substance produce by ants is formic acid, which is the product of oxidation of &quot;a&quot;, means &#39;a&#39; should be formaldehyde. Now, formaldehyde and ketons are prepared by reductive&nbsp;ozonolysis of alkenes. And by oxidation in presence of strong oxidising agents alkenes give ketons and acids.</p></blockquote>"
